      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the difference between sweet paprika and low-heat paprika?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Sweet paprika (under 500 SHU) is made from high-colour sweet pepper varieties like Xinjiang sweet pepper and Red Dragon 23, with an ASTA colour value of 80–180. Low-heat paprika (under 10,000 SHU) comes from varieties like Yidu red and Wangdu, adding mild heat and clear chilli aroma on top of colour."
      }
    },
    {
